    ('160da9ec-9bc4-4893-8066-dd3afb41c5b2'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Chacamarca Historic Sanctuary: 2,500 hectares at approximately 4,105 metres, where patriot forces under Bolivar routed royalist troops on 6 August 1824, protecting Pumpush remains.', NULL, 'teaser-card-s032-rollback:160da9ec-9bc4-4893-8066-dd3afb41c5b2:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s032: card_description None restored on Chacamarca Historic Sanctuary', 'd490003a2468b23516c712f8d321252b55f548dbb1a5f616f374f50c8fcbb39e|ff0c9c9f8a36d7cbd1ee1ddc0f6979c8197ba0b031bf233bce016b6d7fc16ebf|ff0c9c9f8a36d7cbd1ee1ddc0f6979c8197ba0b031bf233bce016b6d7fc16ebf', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: writer teaser-write-003", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Chacamarca Historic Sanctuary: 2,500 hectares at approximately 4,105 metres, where patriot forces under Bolivar routed royalist troops on 6 August 1824, protecting Pumpush remains."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: checker teaser-check-003 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the sanctuary covers 2,500 hectares [S1]; it lies at approximately 4,105 metres above sea level [S1]; patriot forces under Bolivar routed royalist troops [S2]; this happened on 6 August 1824 [S2]; the sanctuary protects Pumpush culture remains [S3]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: verifier teaser-verify-007 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Chacamarca Historic Sanctuary is a protected area in the province of Junin, Peru. [SUPPORTED: https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santuario_hist%C3%B3rico_de_Chacamarca]; The sanctuary covers 2,500 hectares. [SUPPORTED: https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santuario_hist%C3%B3rico_de_Chacamarca]; The sanctuary lies at approximately 4,105 metres above sea level. [SUPPORTED: https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santuario_hist%C3%B3rico_de_Chacamarca]; The sanctuary marks the site of the Battle of Junin. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chacamarca_Historic_Sanctuary]; That battle was fought on 6 August 1824. [SUPPORTED: https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santuario_hist%C3%B3rico_de_Chacamarca]; The patriot forces were led by Simon Bolivar. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Jun%C3%ADn]; The patriot forces routed the royalist troops. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Jun%C3%ADn]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('16818a72-af8e-4397-a814-36c1502b27d3'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Papcastle was Derventio, a Roman fort built in timber and later rebuilt in stone. Excavations from 2010-2015 found one of the most complete Roman water mills in Britain.', NULL, 'teaser-card-s032-rollback:16818a72-af8e-4397-a814-36c1502b27d3:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s032: card_description None restored on Papcastle', '808d107b8e6b934742c782c6a4085e52f078cf91253b9332eea75bf6ff3b70bc|2942ee1bfceb297949667b32a2dcd028afcdf6d1bda643a112c1d50b5e6ac01f|2942ee1bfceb297949667b32a2dcd028afcdf6d1bda643a112c1d50b5e6ac01f', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: writer teaser-write-003", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Papcastle was Derventio, a Roman fort built in timber and later rebuilt in stone. Excavations from 2010-2015 found one of the most complete Roman water mills in Britain."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: checker teaser-check-003 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Papcastle was the site of Derventio, a Roman fort [S1]; the fort was initially built in timber [S2]; it was later reconstructed in stone [S2]; excavations from 2010-2015 took place [S3]; those excavations uncovered one of the most complete Roman water mills found in Britain [S3]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: verifier teaser-verify-007 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Papcastle is the site of a Roman fort. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Derventio_(Papcastle)]; The Roman settlement at Papcastle was known as Derventio. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Derventio_(Papcastle)]; The fort was originally built in timber. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Derventio_(Papcastle)]; The fort was later rebuilt in stone. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Derventio_(Papcastle)]; Excavations were undertaken between 2010 and 2015. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Derventio_(Papcastle)]; Those excavations found one of the most complete Roman water mills yet excavated in Britain. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Derventio_(Papcastle)]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('1758f6e8-4518-43fb-a14a-1ce52caca683'::uuid, 'card_description', 'By the EX-214 road, the Dolmen del prado de Lácara was built toward the end of the 4th millennium BC, or in the early 3rd millennium BC, among Extremadura''s most monumental megalithic sites.', NULL, 'teaser-card-s032-rollback:1758f6e8-4518-43fb-a14a-1ce52caca683:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s032: card_description None restored on Dolmen del prado de Lácara', 'd74b142b3d6ffc5c170ecec1f8a7aae3a2532a6f0e7a5cd5b3aff2a7d07bcfb7|9e9a31ee0c67fd81498fdcf84ec59ae6d09fd263f4465a3d79e592bb27eb152e|9e9a31ee0c67fd81498fdcf84ec59ae6d09fd263f4465a3d79e592bb27eb152e', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: writer teaser-rewrite1-001", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "By the EX-214 road, the Dolmen del prado de Lácara was built toward the end of the 4th millennium BC, or in the early 3rd millennium BC, among Extremadura''s most monumental megalithic sites."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: checker teaser-check1-001 (check1), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the dolmen stands beside the EX-214 road [S1]; it was built toward the end of the 4th millennium BC [S2]; or in the early 3rd millennium BC [S2]; it ranks among the most monumental megalithic sites in Extremadura [S2]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: verifier teaser-verify-007 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Dolmen del prado de Lacara is a megalithic monument, a passage tomb. [SUPPORTED: https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dolmen_del_prado_de_L%C3%A1cara]; The dolmen lies by the EX-214 road. [SUPPORTED: https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dolmen_del_prado_de_L%C3%A1cara]; It was built toward the end of the 4th millennium BC. [SUPPORTED: https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dolmen_del_prado_de_L%C3%A1cara]; It was built in the