It was founded in the mid-4th century BCE [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asclepieion_of_Pergamon]; It began as a modest spring shrine [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asclepieion_of_Pergamon]; It was built up over roughly eight centuries [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asclepieion_of_Pergamon]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('42f11dde-ad7e-46e0-ab7b-37a7add49986'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Drusus founded the Ara trium Galliarum at Lugdunum, where the Rhone and Saone meet, as a sanctuary to Roma and Augustus. Its altar bore the names of 60 Gallic tribes.', NULL, 'teaser-card-s032-rollback:42f11dde-ad7e-46e0-ab7b-37a7add49986:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s032: card_description None restored on Ara trium Galliarum', 'c0643ef668c19a49936a6ef24e6162988afb09b6dbe1248f439696a9c71c67fe|e8719b3ae3b7df58e5706c38ca1577687bbd52197e92ca6b90d87c33161744b4|e8719b3ae3b7df58e5706c38ca1577687bbd52197e92ca6b90d87c33161744b4', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: writer teaser-write-006", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Drusus founded the Ara trium Galliarum at Lugdunum, where the Rhone and Saone meet, as a sanctuary to Roma and Augustus. Its altar bore the names of 60 Gallic tribes."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: checker teaser-check-006 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Drusus founded the Ara trium Galliarum [S1]; it stood at Lugdunum [S1]; it stood at the confluence of the Rhone and Saone [S1]; it was consecrated to Roma and Augustus [S2]; its altar bore the names of 60 Gallic tribes [S3]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: verifier teaser-verify-016 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Ara trium Galliarum was a Roman sanctuary with an altar, near Lugdunum (today Lyon) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ara_trium_Galliarum]; Drusus built the ritual place [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ara_trium_Galliarum]; The sanctuary stood at the confluence of the Saone and the Rhone, at Lugdunum [SUPPORTED: https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanctuaire_f%C3%A9d%C3%A9ral_des_Trois_Gaules]; The altar was consecrated to Roma and Augustus [SUPP